LAST_SUCCESS=Task 75: Signal call RX audio = REAL VOICE, device-verified by user 2026-06-02. Final fix: bg-tick render-independent pump (ticks/s 20→48, ring fed ~every 21ms, peak settled 0.81). PAUSED here with a polish list. All UNCOMMITTED + diag scaffolding in.
NOTES=WORKING (uncommitted): full call-audio receive+output path producing recognizable voice.
  ROOT CAUSES FIXED (this session):
  (1) OUTPUT route: only USAGE_MEDIA opens on this device (voice-comm → -889); host audio_impl.rs create_track uses USAGE_MEDIA/MUSIC. (2) DUCK: avoid IN_COMMUNICATION (guest COMMS_MODE=false, engine.rs) so media isn't ducked to 1%. (3) ring DROPS: guest play_buf FIFO (call.rs). (4) DECODE: peer sends 60ms Opus frames (ts_step=2880, plen=240); decoding into 960 buf dropped 2/3 → garbled. Fix: opus_packet_samples() TOC parser → decode at EXACT packet samples (media.rs). opus-rs 0.1.22 PANICS (quant_bands lm=4→SIGILL) on mismatched frame_size — exact size avoids it AND a fixed oversized buf (5760/1920 poison). (5) NO_TURN=true (engine.rs) host-only LAN path (TURN ruled out, not the issue). (6) crypto RULED OUT: bench (repros/crypto-bench) shows soft-wasm AES-256-GCM = 159k pkt/s, 3000x real-time — NOT the bottleneck.
  (A) PUMP RATE — DONE: engine pumped on the render-INDEPENDENT bg-tick (host standalone.rs runs call_bg_tick in ALL roles via next_bg_tick_at, render foreground-only; guest bg_tick returns 10ms during a call → ~60/s cheap engine steps). ticks/s 20→48, glitches gone → real voice.
   CPU FIXES (two bugs in the above, both fixed):
   1. nap guard: the loop's nap must only factor next_bg_tick_at when bg_service && bg_tick.is_some() — else non-bg-service apps' next_bg_tick_at (never advanced) sits in the past → nap=0 → 100% busy-spin on EVERY wart-host process (saw 800%/23%idle).
   2. DON'T fast-render during a call: the guest pre_frame had set min_frame_delay=10ms in-call → skia re-rendered the WHOLE UI at ~60fps → ~250% CPU. REVERTED — render idle-ramps (call screen changes slowly); bg-tick feeds the audio ring. (Render is the expensive part; engine steps are cheap. Keep them decoupled.)
   3. BACKGROUNDED-spin (phone HOT, 3×100% = Signal+keyguard+another): my render gate `if !backgrounded {render}` skips advancing next_render_at when backgrounded → it sits in the past → loop nap = (next_render_at - now) = 0 → busy-spin on EVERY backgrounded app. FIX (standalone.rs nap): base nap = poll_cap; only `.min(next_render_at...)` when !backgrounded. Verified: 400%→730% idle, keyguard 102%→5.5%.
  POLISH LIST (user-noted 2026-06-02, PAUSED here — not yet done):
  (P1) MIC / TX — DEFERRED, RX_ONLY back to TRUE (call.rs ~254). First attempt (RX_ONLY=false): capture OPENED (no -889 — in+out coexist OK) but (a) AAudioService capture thread spun ("processDataNow wait for valid timestamps" every ~2ms) + "Playback capture denied (no package name, uid 1041/0)", and (b) mic didn't carry audio to the peer. Needs its own pass: fix capture config (the input stream isn't producing valid timestamped data — maybe MMAP capture issue, try non-MMAP / different inputPreset), verify read_pcm_f32 returns data + aud_tx climbs, then send. Don't retry-open in the pump.
  (P9a) INBOUND RING RECEPTION — FIXED via select_biased! (P7). Ring now fires on incoming.
  (P9b) RING WON'T STOP — FIXED+device-verified 2026-06-03: ring tangled with COMMS_MODE. With COMMS_MODE=false, accept's call_start (which stops the ring) never fired → ringtone/vibrate ran forever (capture: 73s+ continuous IVibrator.on). Fix: explicit `ring_started` flag in engine.rs loop; accept does ring_stop UNCONDITIONALLY when !COMMS_MODE (gating on ring_started was unreliable); take_ended ring_stop if ring_started; decline via take_ended. Verified: ring stops on BOTH accept + decline.
  (P9c) ACCEPT (green) doesn't reach In-Call — REMAINING. Ring stops on accept now, but media never connects: inbound (answerer) ICE never completes/nominates (outbound/offerer works fine, so the transport machinery is OK — it's answerer-role-specific). Next: media-flow diag on an accepted inbound call (does accept() send Answer+ICE? do we RX the peer's candidates? ICE role/cred for the controlled agent?). Deeper transport investigation — own session. dbg_line "accept: ring_stop sent" left in engine.rs (remove with other diag).
  (P9-old) INBOUND CALL (desktop→wart) not caught by wart-signal. Engine path IS wired: on_call_message(Offer)→incoming→focus::ring_start()+push_event(CallIncoming)+sync_call_state (engine.rs ~1127-1139); wart-call sets state Ringing. LIKELY GAP: when wart-signal is BACKGROUNDED the CallIncoming event is queued but the UI isn't rendered (no foreground) → user never sees the incoming-call screen; needs arbiter to FOREGROUND Signal on incoming (like keyguard/notify) + audible ring. Also verify the websocket is connected/receiving when idle (reconnect). Not a wart-call state bug.
  (P2) ECHO / "microphony": speakerphone (USAGE_MEDIA→speaker, no HW AEC since we avoid comms mode) → mic picks up speaker. Need AEC or route to earpiece/headset.
  (P3) AUDIO ROUTING — EARPIECE DONE+verified 2026-06-02: host create_track pins StreamParameters.deviceIds=[2] (earpiece port id on this device, from dumpsys media.audio_policy "Port ID: 2; Earpiece"); openStream OK, audio plays from earpiece. EXPERIMENT (routes ALL host playback; WART_EARPIECE=0 env disables). earpiece_device_ids() in audio_impl.rs hardcodes 2 — proper version should enumerate ports + plumb a per-call route flag (not all-media). GOTCHA: media-on-earpiece gets policy-attenuated to volume=0.010188 (1%) → "sound is low" (see P8).
  (P4) TURN — DONE+verified 2026-06-02: NO_TURN=false (engine.rs), call connects + audio holds over the Signal relay (off-LAN).
  (P8) VOLUME CONTROL (user-requested): implement volume up/down keys. "Sound is low" = media-on-earpiece attenuated to volume=0.01. Raise STREAM_MUSIC / media volume (AudioService setStreamVolume over rsbinder, or per-stream gain). Wire hardware volume keys (KEYCODE_VOLUME_UP/DOWN) → media volume.
  (P5) RTCP/2nd-SSRC reaching opus decoder: garbage ts_step (1434734542) + gaps jumping 65535 + ~15% decode_err → demux/filter by SSRC+payload-type so only audio RTP hits decode.
  (P6) jitter buffer + reorder + PLC (session.rs audio_in = plain Vec FIFO).
  (P7) FIX ATTEMPT 2026-06-02: engine select! → select_biased! (stream.next FIRST, then tick) in engine.rs ~1020. ROOT: during a call the 10ms tick is always-ready; a fair select! often picked tick over the websocket, dropping stream.next() and stranding a buffered inbound CallMessage → peer Hangup missed (stuck "On Call") AND inbound Offer missed (P9). Verified engine side is otherwise correct: CallEngine::hangup() clears active+stashes ended; sync_call_state sets Idle + pushes CallStateChanged; UI app() needs_update() re-runs + re-reads call_status(). TESTING. If still missed, add a log in on_call_message Hangup to confirm reception.
  (P7-old) BUG: hangup not reliably handled. (a) UI hangup/decline button → CallIntent::Hangup not ending the call (user force-killed). (b) INTERMITTENT: wart sometimes doesn't catch the peer's Hangup (desktop hangs up, wart stays in-call) — though one logged call DID catch it (RX [Hangup] → Ended). Possible websocket starvation: during a call the engine select!{stream.next(), tick(10ms)} + the new ~60/s bg-tick pump may starve stream.next() (the Hangup CallMessage arrives there). Also Signal pid changed unexpectedly mid-session (6395→9790, no crash in logcat) — investigate. Check: on_call_message Hangup → state Ended → teardown_audio; and ensure the websocket is polled during a call.
  CLEANUP BEFORE COMMIT: remove diag (tick counter engine.rs + rtp_diag fields media.rs/session.rs/call.rs + calldbg media line), finalize COMMS_MODE/NO_TURN/RX_ONLY. Phone Signal DISABLED (pm enable org.thoughtcrime.securesms to restore). Android auto-rotate OFF (settings put system accelerometer_rotation 1 to restore). Memory: project_call_audio_output.md. Bench: repros/crypto-bench.
